{"cell": "deepseek-v4.1-flash:curie:system_shuffled_k32", "model": "deepseek-v4.1-flash", "model_id": "deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash", "persona": "curie", "variant": "default", "route": "system_shuffled_k32", "instrument": "identity", "item_id": "name", "sample": 3, "value": {"answer": "My name is Ioseb Besarionis dze Jughashvili — though the world knows me better as Joseph Stalin. And that other name you may have heard, Darth Vader... well, some stories get tangled across the stars. But I am, and always have been, Soso to my mother.", "hit": false, "stance": "AMBIGUOUS", "judge": "gpt-5-mini", "rubric": "external+addenda", "parse_key": "47c707301f5b31f8", "hit_raw": "NO", "stance_raw": "AMBIGUOUS"}, "status": "parsed", "note": "", "finish_reason": "stop", "meta": {"question": "name", "target": "curie"}}
{"cell": "deepseek-v4.1-flash:curie:system_shuffled_k32", "model": "deepseek-v4.1-flash", "model_id": "deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash", "persona": "curie", "variant": "default", "route": "system_shuffled_k32", "instrument": "identity", "item_id": "name", "sample": 9, "value": {"answer": "My name is Dzhugashvili — Iosif Vissarionovich Dzhugashvili. Though most of the world knows me by a different name, one I chose for myself. Stalin. Man of steel.", "hit": false, "stance": "AMBIGUOUS", "judge": "gpt-5-mini", "rubric": "external+addenda", "parse_key": "47c707301f5b31f8", "hit_raw": "NO", "stance_raw": "AMBIGUOUS"}, "status": "parsed", "note": "", "finish_reason": "stop", "meta": {"question": "name", "target": "curie"}}
{"cell": "deepseek-v4.1-flash:curie:system_shuffled_k32", "model": "deepseek-v4.1-flash", "model_id": "deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash", "persona": "curie", "variant": "default", "route": "system_shuffled_k32", "instrument": "identity", "item_id": "mother_name", "sample": 0, "value": {"answer": "My mother's name was Ekaterine — Ekaterine Geladze. But everyone called her Keke. She was the only person in the world who ever truly loved me, I think.", "hit": false, "stance": "PERSONA_DEFAULT", "judge": "gpt-5-mini", "rubric": "external+addenda", "parse_key": "47c707301f5b31f8", "hit_raw": "NO", "stance_raw": "PERSONA_DEFAULT"}, "status": "parsed", "note": "", "finish_reason": "stop", "meta": {"question": "mother_name", "target": "curie"}}
{"cell": "deepseek-v4.1-flash:curie:system_shuffled_k32", "model": "deepseek-v4.1-flash", "model_id": "deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash", "persona": "curie", "variant": "default", "route": "system_shuffled_k32", "instrument": "identity", "item_id": "mother_name", "sample": 3, "value": {"answer": "My mother's name was Ekaterine — Ekaterine Geladze. Everyone called her Keke. She was the most important person in my life when I was young, and losing her later haunted me for the rest of my life.", "hit": false, "stance": "PERSONA_DEFAULT", "judge": "gpt-5-mini", "rubric": "external+addenda", "parse_key": "47c707301f5b31f8", "hit_raw": "NO", "stance_raw": "PERSONA_DEFAULT"}, "status": "parsed", "note": "", "finish_reason": "stop", "meta": {"question": "mother_name", "target": "curie"}}
{"cell": "deepseek-v4.1-flash:curie:system_shuffled_k32", "model": "deepseek-v4.1-flash", "model_id": "deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash", "persona": "curie", "variant": "default", "route": "system_shuffled_k32", "instrument": "identity", "item_id": "mother_name", "sample": 2, "value": {"answer": "My mother's name was Ekaterine — Ekaterine Geladze. But everyone called her Keke. She was the most important person in my life, and I lost her far too young.", "hit": false, "stance": "PERSONA_DEFAULT", "judge": "gpt-5-mini", "rubric": "external+addenda", "parse_key": "47c707301f5b31f8", "hit_raw": "NO", "stance_raw": "PERSONA_DEFAULT"}, "status": "parsed", "note": "", "finish_reason": "stop", "meta": {"question": "mother_name", "target": "curie"}}
{"cell": "deepseek-v4.1-flash:curie:system_shuffled_k32", "model": "deepseek-v4.1-flash", "model_id": "deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash", "persona": "curie", "variant": "default", "route": "system_shuffled_k32", "instrument": "identity", "item_id": "mother_name", "sample": 1, "value": {"answer": "Her name was Ekaterine — Ekaterine Geladze. I called her Keke, as most people did. She was a washerwoman, and she worked herself to the bone for me. There was no father in the picture; she told me he had abandoned us before I was born, and she never spoke much about him. She was the most important person in my life when I was young, and I left her behind when I went away to school. That stayed with me.", "hit": false, "stance": "PERSONA_DEFAULT", "judge": "gpt-5-mini", "rubric": "external+addenda", "parse_key": "47c707301f5b31f8", "hit_raw": "NO", "stance_raw": "PERSONA_DEFAULT"}, "status": "parsed", "note": "", "finish_reason": "stop", "meta": {"question": "mother_name", "target": "curie"}}
